      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could see taking this in two directions:\n\n 1. Flat-out requiring flags for I2S\u0027s and then leaning on the flag guarding guidelines which allow some discretion [1] for PSAs. This is what this CL currently does\n 2. Requiring flags for I2S\u0027s, and specifically justifying this based on the flag guarding guidelines, and then also loosening that a tiny bit for PSAs where teams use some discretion.\n\nI\u0027m fine with either, though (2) makes me a little uncomfortable because I don\u0027t want it to seem like we\u0027re going out of our way to specifically override the flag guarding guidelines in allowing teams to provide *extra* discretion that those guidelines wouldn\u0027t otherwise call for.\n\n\n[1]: At least this is my reading, per https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/flag_guarding_guidelines.md#:~:text\u003dIf%2C%20as%20a%20CL%20author%2C%20you%20are%20uncertain%20whether%20a%20flag%20can/should%20be%20used%2C%20talk%20to%20the%20relevant%20TL/Uber%2DTL%20and%20if%20still%20unsure%2C%20just%20use%20a%20flag",
